  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.4. Increased capacity of Member States to improve social dialogue and labour relations laws, processes and institutions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following a bipartite training conducted in April  2022 with negotiators from 9 public service associations and 5 government ministries in Botswana, three collective agreements were concluded for 2022-25 covering workers in general public service, education and health. The ILO provided technical support, policy advice and capacity building to the bipartite partners throughout the biennium. 
A training workshop on mutual gains bargaining and on team building was conducted in April 2022</narrative>
   </description>
